From: mh2lm clock work <clock@mh2lm>
Subject: [PATCH 0238] clock: the PDM gate's parent is XO, and the counter said so

0130 shipped C2-03 with gcc_pdm_xo4_clk declared as a child of the fixed XO/4
reference clock. The name reads that way, the vendor branch at 0x33008 has no
parent to contradict it, and the C2-08 counter reference at 0x43008 really is
an XO/4 branch, so the descriptor mirrored what the tree already described.

The device disagreed. sweetlog-0130-1, the ring that ran the gate and the
measurement together, measured the branch it had just enabled at 19200036 Hz
while the descriptor declared 4800000: a delta of 3000007 ppm, reported as
BadArgument instead of a pass. The same ring measured both controls as
expected - gcc_disp_xo_clk at 19199963 (delta -1 ppm), gcc_pdm2_clk at 0 with
equal short and full counts - so neither the counter nor its /4 timebase was
at fault. The branch outputs the XO clock; the "xo4" in its name is not a
divider.

The vendor tree agrees once the branch is read as the clk_branch2 gate it is:
debugcc-sm8150.c's MUX_SRC_LIST maps debug index 0x99 to gcc_pdm_xo4_clk, the
branch at 0x33008 carries enable_mask = BIT(0) and clk_branch2_ops with no
.parent_names and no divider field, and its sibling gcc_disp_xo_clk, which the
device measures at 19200000, is parentless in exactly the same way. A branch
with no parent name cannot divide its parent, and the only /4 in this system
is the counter's own timebase at 0x43008 (localID 7).

So localID 4 becomes a child of kIOQcomSourceXO and kIOQcomGccGateHz becomes
19200000, while localID 7 stays the tree's only XO/4 identity. That is what
makes the C2-03 sample a real cross-check rather than the tautology it was in
0130: descriptor and counter now have to agree about two different clocks. The
rate formula keeps 4800000, because that constant is the counter's calibration,
not a claim about the measured branch.

The host fixture follows the device: the counter model returns four counts per
loaded XO/4 tick when 0x99 is selected, the branch state and the provider
contract expect the XO rate, the gate+measure case asserts the comparison row
against the C2-02 decoding, and the gate-only case pins the read cost the 0130
ring printed - 11 snapshot + 2 + 6 walk + 1 request + 1 poll + 8 neighbours =
29 - so the auditor's expected count stays a derived sum and not a guess.

The fixture can also print those rows on request (MH2LM_GCC_DUMP_ROWS=1), so the
offline ring auditor re-reads the rows this very build produced rather than a
hand-written sample of the vocabulary. The shipped run is unchanged.

